<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Bern</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">founded 1710</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">New Bern is a town in eastern North Carolina founded in 1710 by Swiss and German settlers under Christoph von Graffenried at the meeting of the Neuse and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trento">Trent</a> rivers. Its encroachment on Tuscarora land helped provoke the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuscarora-war">Tuscarora War</a> of 1711. It later became the capital of the Province of North Carolina, where Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-tryon">William Tryon</a> built his palace.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/new-bern.jpg" alt="New Bern" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tradewinds · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Bern_Municipal_Building_(City_Hall).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
